Assertions:
1. evaluated in observed region
2. assertions are evaluated based on sampled value
3. sampled value of a variable is its value in prepone region
4. if the same variable is used as expression for clock and to evaluate the assertion, the result might be different since the assertion is triggered at the variable's current value while the assertion uses
   the sampled value.
5. A property may involve checking of one or more sequential behaviors beginning at various times
6. $
7. ##[*]
8. ##[+]
9. [*]
10.[=]
11.[->]
12.throughout
13.within
14.intersect
15.and
16.or


Example:
C1: cover property (@(posedge clk) mycond);
sequence seq1;
@(posedge clk) 1;
endsequence
C2: cover property (@seq1 mycond);
// fastclk is a clock driven at 2x the frequency of clk
sequence seq2;
@(posedge fastclk) !clk ##1 clk;
endsequence
C3: cover property (@seq2 mycond);

Example
bit a;
integer b;
byte q[$];
property p1;
$rose(a) |-> q[0];
endproperty
property p2;
integer l_b;
($rose(a), l_b = b) |-> ##[3:10] q[l_b];
endproperty

